# Water

Gold standard: [Evan Wallace's WebGL water](https://madebyevan.com/webgl-water/)
([caustics](https://medium.com/@evanwallace/rendering-realtime-caustics-in-webgl-2a99a29a0b2c),
[source](https://github.com/evanw/webgl-water)). Puddles must **look and behave** like that demo.
A flat sheet, a tint, or a shader-only ripple is a regression.

## Look (optics)

- Tessellated **vertex-displaced** surface from a heightfield `(h, v, n.x, n.z)`.
- **Shading normals come from the field**, never from noise alone. Noise is detail on the normal;
  if the cube's dimple and wake do not change the lighting, the water is still a sticker.
- Peaked normals (Wallace walks the sample along `n.xz`). IOR air 1 / water 1.333.
- Fresnel mix of the **refracted pool floor** and the reflected sky, plus a sun spec.
- Caustics are Jacobian (`oldArea/newArea` in **world xz**, one field texel apart) and belong
  **on the pool floor**, not painted on the surface. Never `dFdx`/`dFdy`: those follow the
  camera's pixel axes and hatch diagonally under the quarter-turn yaw. A light-space caustic
  target is allowed but not required. Field samples pin `level(0)` so the tessellated film
  cannot hatch from implicit LOD either.
- The surface film is **thin face-on** (`WATER_SURFACE_ALPHA`) so the floor and the submerged cube
  read through it, and opaque at grazing angles.
- Below-water pass is deferred, not rejected: this camera cannot submerge under a 0.38 puddle, so
  it would be dead code. Add it with the first swimmable body of water.
- Palette stays earned teal `#2e5461`, distinct from ice, never near-white on this world.

## Behave (coupling)

- Wave equation, ping-pong: `v += (avg(h) − h) * 2; v *= 0.995; h += v`.
- Cube occupancy uses Wallace `moveSphere` (add old volume, subtract new).
- Land / splash is `addDrop`.
- Visual Y uses Wallace sphere physics: `percentUnderWater`, reduced gravity, quadratic drag.
  **Cell, orientation, and camera rest-height stay on the lattice.** Waves never shake the camera.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — film on the cell
stampSheets(scene, waterMat, lift: 0.012);

// ✅ GOOD — volume the cube occupies, field carves around it
field.coupleCube(cube.x, cube.y, cube.z, waterPlaneY, inWater);
material.positionNode = positionLocal.add(vec3(0, 0, fieldHeight));
```

## Allowed / forbidden

- **Allowed in render:** GPU or CPU heightfield, vertex displacement, caustic RTT, two-pass water,
  buoyancy/drag on visual Y. TSL only (`ShaderMaterial` is dead under `WebGPURenderer`).
- **Forbidden:** reading the field back into sim; putting the clock uniform in both stages;
  analog xz / ori; camera following wave height.
- Clock stays fragment-owned (`onFrameUpdate`). Displacement must not sample that clock.
- Reduced motion freezes ripples and physics; the dimple and waterline stay.

See ADR 0013 and `.cursor/rules/canon.mdc`.
